        "text": "Yes. Indiana became the 41st Agreement State on 1 October 2026, with the Indiana Department of Homeland Security's Radioactive Materials Control Program taking over most radioactive-materials licensing from the NRC. Because the change is new, confirm the current licensing authority with the state before radiography work."
